# Auth: what's left

Do the steps in order.

{{- if .EnvKeys}}

## 1. Config

In `internal/config/config.go`, import `{{.GoModule}}/internal/auth` and add:

```go
// add to Config
Auth auth.AuthConfig

// add to NewConfig()
Auth: auth.NewAuthConfig(),
```
{{- end}}

## {{if .EnvKeys}}2{{else}}1{{end}}. DI

In `internal/di/di.go`, add to `Di`:

```go
Auth          appauth.AuthService
Authenticate  {{if .Grpc}}connect.Interceptor{{else}}func(http.Handler) http.Handler{{end}} // use it on your own routes too
AuthRateLimit {{if .Grpc}}connect.Interceptor{{else}}func(http.Handler) http.Handler{{end}}
```

Imports:

```go
{{- if .Mfa}}
"encoding/hex"
{{- end}}
{{- if not .Grpc}}
"net/http"
{{- end}}
"time"
{{- if .Grpc}}
"connectrpc.com/connect"
{{- end}}
"github.com/nayefradwi/nayef_go_common/auth"
"github.com/nayefradwi/nayef_go_common/auth/{{.StorePkg}}"
{{- if .Grpc}}
"github.com/nayefradwi/nayef_go_common/auth/authconnect"
{{- else}}
"github.com/nayefradwi/nayef_go_common/auth/authhttp"
{{- end}}
"github.com/nayefradwi/nayef_go_common/errors"
appauth "{{.GoModule}}/internal/auth"
```

Add this to `RegisterServices()`, after the {{if .Redis}}database and Redis connections are{{else}}database connection is{{end}} made. You can change any limit or time below.
{{- if .Jwt}}

**Logout does not end access tokens.** An access token keeps working until it expires (15 minutes below). Logout only ends the refresh token.
{{- end}}

```go
sessionStore := errors.Must({{.StorePkg}}.NewSessionStore(di.{{.StoreDiField}}))
codeStore := errors.Must({{.StorePkg}}.NewCodeStore(di.{{.StoreDiField}}))
attemptStore := {{.StorePkg}}.NewAttemptStore(di.{{.StoreDiField}})
{{- if .Mfa}}
totpStore := errors.Must({{.StorePkg}}.NewTotpStore(di.{{.StoreDiField}}))
{{- end}}
{{- if .Jwt}}
provider := auth.NewJwtTokenProvider(errors.Must(auth.NewJwtTokenProviderConfig(config.Auth.JwtSecret, 15*time.Minute, auth.AccessTokenType)))
sessions := errors.Must(auth.NewJwtSessionManager(sessionStore, provider, 30*24*time.Hour))
{{- else}}
sessions := errors.Must(auth.NewOpaqueSessionManager(sessionStore, 15*time.Minute, 30*24*time.Hour))
{{- end}}
{{- if .Grpc}}
di.Authenticate = authconnect.{{if .Jwt}}NewJwtInterceptor(provider){{else}}NewOpaqueInterceptor(sessions){{end}}
di.AuthRateLimit = authconnect.RateLimit(errors.Must(auth.NewLimiter(attemptStore, 20, time.Hour)), authconnect.ByIP("codes"))
{{- else}}
di.Authenticate = authhttp.{{if .Jwt}}NewJwtMiddleware(provider){{else}}NewOpaqueMiddleware(sessions){{end}}.UseAuthentication
di.AuthRateLimit = authhttp.RateLimit(errors.Must(auth.NewLimiter(attemptStore, 20, time.Hour)), authhttp.ByIP("codes"))
{{- end}}
{{- if .Password}}
logins := errors.Must(auth.NewLimiter(attemptStore, 5, 15*time.Minute))
resets := errors.Must(auth.NewOneTimeTokenManager(codeStore, auth.CodeLimits{
	TTL: 30 * time.Minute, ResendAfter: time.Minute, MaxSends: 3, MaxAttempts: 5,
}))
{{- end}}
{{- if .Otp}}
codes := errors.Must(auth.NewOtpManager(codeStore, auth.OtpConfig{
	Secret:     []byte(config.Auth.OtpSecret),
	Length:     6,
	CodeLimits: auth.CodeLimits{TTL: 10 * time.Minute, ResendAfter: time.Minute, MaxSends: 5, MaxAttempts: 5},
}))
{{- end}}
{{- if .Mfa}}
totp := errors.Must(auth.NewTotpManager(totpStore, auth.TotpConfig{
	Key:    errors.Must(hex.DecodeString(config.Auth.TotpKey)),
	Issuer: "{{.ProjectName}}",
}))
pending := errors.Must(auth.NewOneTimeTokenManager(codeStore, auth.CodeLimits{
	TTL: 5 * time.Minute, ResendAfter: 0, MaxSends: 5, MaxAttempts: 5,
}))
{{- end}}
di.Auth = appauth.NewAuthService(di.Pool, sessions
{{- if .Password}}, logins, resets, auth.DefaultPasswordPolicy, auth.DefaultHashingConfig{{end}}
{{- if .Otp}}, codes{{end}}
{{- if .Mfa}}, totp, pending{{end -}}
)
```

## {{if .EnvKeys}}3{{else}}2{{end}}. Router
{{- if .Grpc}}

In `cmd/api/router.go`, import `appauth "{{.GoModule}}/internal/auth"` and `{{.GoModule}}/gen/auth/v1/authv1connect`. Add to `setup()`:

```go
authHandler := appauth.NewAuthHandler(ar.di.Auth)
ar.mux.Handle(authv1connect.NewAuthServiceHandler(authHandler, opts))
limited := connect.WithHandlerOptions(opts, connect.WithInterceptors(ar.di.AuthRateLimit))
ar.mux.Handle(authv1connect.NewCodeServiceHandler(authHandler, limited))
authed := connect.WithHandlerOptions(opts, connect.WithInterceptors(ar.di.Authenticate))
ar.mux.Handle(authv1connect.NewAccountServiceHandler(authHandler, authed))
```

To protect your own services, use `authed`. To allow only some users, add `connect.WithInterceptors(authconnect.VerifyClaim("role", "admin"))`.

In `internal/health/handler.go`, add to `NewStaticChecker`:

```go
authv1connect.AuthServiceName, authv1connect.CodeServiceName, authv1connect.AccountServiceName
```
{{- else}}

In `cmd/api/router.go`, import `appauth "{{.GoModule}}/internal/auth"`. Add to `setup()`:

```go
ar.mux.Mount("/auth", appauth.NewAuthHandler(ar.di.Auth).Routes(ar.di.Authenticate, ar.di.AuthRateLimit))

// protect your own routes
ar.mux.Group(func(r chi.Router) {
	r.Use(ar.di.Authenticate)
	r.Use(authhttp.VerifyClaim("role", "admin")) // optional
})
```
{{- end}}
{{- if .EnvKeys}}

## 4. Secrets

Your local `.env` already has values for {{range $i, $k := .EnvKeys}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}`{{$k}}`{{end}}.

Every deployed environment needs its own values. **Do not copy the values from your local `.env`.** Make a new one for each key:

```sh
openssl rand -hex 32
```
{{- if .Mfa}}

**Never change `TOTP_KEY` after users turn on MFA.** It encrypts their MFA secrets. A new key breaks MFA for every user.
{{- end}}

Where to put them: open `deployments/<env>/TODO.md` and follow "Add your own environment variables". Treat each key as a secret.
{{- end}}

## {{if .EnvKeys}}5{{else}}3{{end}}. Database

Run `goose up` on your computer. Deployed environments run it on every deploy.
{{- if .Redis}}

Redis holds sessions, codes{{if .Mfa}}, login attempts and MFA secrets{{else}} and login attempts{{end}}. Your Redis must have:

- version 7 or newer, not Cluster mode
- persistence turned on
- `maxmemory-policy noeviction`

**If Redis drops data, users are logged out{{if .Mfa}} and lose MFA{{end}}.**
{{- else}}

Expired sessions, codes and attempts stay in the database. To clean them up, run `DeleteExpired` on the session, code and attempt stores on a schedule.
{{- end}}

